  "summary_en": "The OAIC's Australian Privacy Principles Guidelines (combined, July 2019) explain the Information Commissioner's interpretation of the 13 APPs under the Privacy Act 1988. They are non-binding guidance on collection, use, disclosure, security, access and correction of personal information. The file does not match the AI-products guidance named in its title and has no AI or robotics content.",
  "key_provisions_or_claims": [
   "APP guidelines are issued under s 28(1) of the Privacy Act and are not legally binding.",
   "APP 6 allows use or disclosure of personal information only for the primary purpose unless an exception applies.",
   "APPs are principles-based and technology neutral.",
   "APP 13 requires a response to correction requests within 30 days and bars charges for correction.",
   "The guidelines cover APPs 1-13 across the personal information lifecycle."
